{{also|lineup|line-up}}
==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|En-ca-lineup.ogg|Audio (CA)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{legal}} a physical or photographic queue of people allegedly involved in a crime
# {{Canada}} A line of people or vehicles, in which the individual at the front end is dealt with first, the one behind is dealt with next, and so on, and in which newcomers join at the end.
# {{sports}} Collectively, the members of a [[team]].
#:''The manager fielded his strongest line-up for the game against United.''
# {{baseball}} The [[batting order]].

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|line of people or vehicles}} {{qualifier|American}} [[line]], {{qualifier|British}} [[queue]]
* {{sense|row of people for identifying a suspect}} {{qualifier|British}} [[identity parade]]

===Verb===
{{en-verb|inf=[[line]] [[up]]|lines up|lining up|lined up}}

# {{engineering}} to put in alignment; to put in correct adjustment for smooth running
# {{transitive}} To put things in a [[line]]
# {{intransitive}} To get into a [[line]]
# {{intransitive|sport}} To [[start]] a game in a certain position on the playing field.
